 and see how the game progresses.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: The player holds a Rocket (Black Joker + Red Joker), a strong pair (KK), and three unconnected small singles (5, 6, 10). With all 2s removed from the game (played in previous turn), the Aces are the highest ranking standard cards held by opponents. The primary goal is to offload the three weak singles. Playing the Rocket or Kings immediately is suboptimal because it would leave the player with weak singles and no way to regain control if the opponents take the lead and run sequences or pairs. By playing a small single (5), the player initiates the process of clearing junk cards and forces opponents to use their high cards (Aces) to win the trick. The player retains the Pair of Kings (which is very strong as only AA can beat it) and the Rocket (invincible) as two separate control mechanisms to regain the initiative later.\n\nReason: You have three weak singles (5, 6, 10) that need to be cleared. Playing the lowest single is the standard opening to probe opponents and preserve your control cards (KK and Rocket) for critical moments or to regain the lead.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥5"]}'}
